  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>Acetaminophen is a common pain reliever and fever reducer. Here is a graph showing the amount of acetaminophen, in milligrams, in an adult’s body at different times after they take a normal dose.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Graph of an exponential function, origin O. time (hours) and acetaminophen (mg)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6067169e5114ec7c6decefb23c92843d3d582b07"/></media></figure></para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Answer the following questions.
        <para> What is the vertical intercept?</para>
        </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> 1,000 </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> What does it mean in this situation?</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>There are 1,000 mg of acetaminophen in the person’s body after taking the medicine (this is the dose size). </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> What fraction of the medicine remained after one hour? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(\frac34\) of the medicine remained after 1 hour since \(\frac{750}{1000}=\frac{3}{4}\). </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Write an equation that represents the amount of medicine, \(a\), after \(t\) hours. </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
    </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para> \(a=1,000(\frac{3}{4})^t\) </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End --></section>
